  "decision_conditions": [
    "The unauthorised development would provide a poor standard of accommodation for future occupiers. Insufficient information has been submitted to demonstrate compliance with internal space standards, minimum floor-to-ceiling height requirements and the functionality of the proposed residential layouts. Furthermore, inadequate private amenity space would be provided for the one-bedroom dwelling. The development therefore conflicts with Policy D6 of the London Plan, Core Policy 4 of the Enfield Core Strategy, Policies DMD8 and DMD9 of the Enfield Development Management Document, and the Nationally Described Space Standards.\r",
    "The unauthorised development, by reason of its poor design, lack of supporting information and unsatisfactory relationship with the servicing arrangements associated with the ground floor commercial unit, fails to demonstrate that it would provide a high quality and functional living environment for future occupiers or preserve the effective operation of the commercial premises. The development is therefore contrary to Paragraph 139 of the National Planning Policy Framework, Core Policy 30 of the Enfield Core Strategy and Policies DMD6, DMD8, DMD30 and DMD37 of the Enfield Development Management Document.",
    "The unauthorised development would fail to demonstrate that safe and suitable access, parking and cycle parking arrangements can be provided. The proposed layout would give rise to conflict between pedestrians and vehicles within the rear service area, whilst the residential entrances would open directly onto the service road, creating an unacceptable highway environment. Furthermore, insufficient information has been submitted to assess the impact of overspill parking or to demonstrate the provision of policy-compliant cycle parking. The development is therefore contrary to Paragraphs 116 and 117 of the National Planning Policy Framework, Policies T4, T5 and T6.1 of the London Plan, and Policies DMD45 and DMD47 of the Enfield Development Management Document.",
    "The unauthorised development would fail to demonstrate that adequate refuse and recycling storage and collection facilities can be provided to serve the proposed residential accommodation. As a result, the development would fail to provide a satisfactory living environment for future occupiers and would prejudice the effective operation of the site. The development is therefore contrary to Chapter 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework, Policy SI7 of the London Plan, Core Policy 22 of the Enfield Core Strategy, and Policies DMD8, DMD30, DMD47 and DMD82 of the Enfield Development Management Document."
  ],
